    "prompt": "Explain why the sky is blue.",
    "chosen": "The sky appears blue due to a phenomenon called Rayleigh scattering.\n\n1. Sunlight contains all colors of the visible spectrum\n2. When sunlight enters Earth's atmosphere, it collides with gas molecules\n3. Shorter wavelengths (blue and violet) scatter more than longer wavelengths (red and orange)\n4. Blue light scatters approximately 5.5 times more than red light\n5. Although violet scatters even more, our eyes are more sensitive to blue, and some violet is absorbed in the upper atmosphere\n\nThis is why we perceive the sky as blue during the day.",
